{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107760","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107760/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107760/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107760/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107760","id":3163085356,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6bZ9Hz","number":107760,"title":"Add `RETURN_IF_ERR` macro, propagating an error upwards","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"aaccff","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2304948121,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzA0OTQ4MTIx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:codestyle","name":"topic:codestyle","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2025-06-20T12:01:57Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T19:17:53Z","closed_at":"2026-09-17T19:13:46Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107760","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107760","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107760.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107760.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Godot does not use exceptions. This often results in patterns where errors are _propagated upwards_:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nError error = expression();\r\nif (error) {\r\n\treturn error;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI propose to support this paradigm with a dedicated macro:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nRETURN_IF_ERROR(expression());\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe benefit of this is threefold:\r\n- Error propagation is encouraged (through the 'syntactic sugar').\r\n- Existing code is (arguably) easier to read than before.\r\n- The code is standardized, and if desired, could be improved (e.g. by adding more printing).\r\n\r\nAn arguable downside is that it's 'another godot-thing' to remember about the code base. I personally think the naming makes it clear enough what the macro does, though.\r\n\r\n## Relations\r\n\r\nThe idea of this macro may be familiar to Rust programmers. Rust embraces exception-free coding so much it made this concept into a core part of its grammar, with the [question mark ? operator](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-example/std/result/question_mark.html).\r\nIt [has been proposed](https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/papers/2022/p2561r0.html) to add this operator to C++ too, for exception-free projects like Godot, but it's unlikely it will make it into the standard anytime soon.","closed_by":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107760/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107760/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}